A thread bound to units is not settled: it joins no queue, and its account is not held to what the new units hold.
A ready thread would never get the processor, and one moved to fewer units would keep what it saved under more;
every ready thread but the running one that may run waits on the queue its account and binding say,
and no account holds more than its cap.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: thread's account holds more than its cap

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -443,7 +443,6 @@ void sched_bind(struct thread *t, uint32_t first, uint32_t count, uint8_t rights
     }
     /* What the account held stays, and settling holds it to what the new units hold at most. */
     t->balance = kept;
-    lender_settle(t);
 }
 
 void sched_unbind(struct cap *bound)
